WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.554
Danny: What do you mean Chuck and Dave are in prison?

2
00:00:03.555 --> 00:00:05.221
Brad: Just what I said.

3
00:00:05.222 --> 00:00:07.526
The mites have locked them up.

4
00:00:07.528 --> 00:00:13.113
Danny: Well, if we can't get them out, maybe we should

5
00:00:13.114 --> 00:00:15.798
leave. Brad: Do you want to stay small

6
00:00:15.799 --> 00:00:17.128
forever? Danny:

7
00:00:17.129 --> 00:00:18.953
No. Brad: We need Chuck and

8
00:00:18.954 --> 00:00:23.350
Dave. They are our only clue how to get us all back to normal.

9
00:00:23.351 --> 00:00:26.907
Danny: Well, I'm not going to stay small

10
00:00:26.908 --> 00:00:36.090
forever! Hold the straw steady—I'm coming up!

11
00:00:36.092 --> 00:00:38.785
Wow! You were right. There

12
00:00:38.786 --> 00:00:41.267
are a lot of mites! Brad:

13
00:00:41.268 --> 00:00:43.106
I know. Danny:

14
00:00:43.107 --> 00:00:48.771
So where are Chuck and Dave? What

15
00:00:48.772 --> 00:00:51.522
are we going to do? Brad: I

16
00:00:51.523 --> 00:00:52.881
don't know. We

17
00:00:52.882 --> 00:00:55.762
have got to get them out somehow. Danny:

18
00:00:55.763 --> 00:01:00.005
Okay. Mites. What are mites? Brad:

19
00:01:00.006 --> 00:01:05.706
Well, mites are small gross things. Danny:

20
00:01:05.707 --> 00:01:07.858
Besides that. Brad:

21
00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:10.823
They're invertebrates. Danny:

22
00:01:10.824 --> 00:01:13.714
Cool. What does that mean? Brad:

23
00:01:13.715 --> 00:01:15.539
They don't have spines. All

24
00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.061
insects are invertebrates. Danny:

25
00:01:19.062 --> 00:01:21.054
How does that help us?

26
00:01:21.055 --> 00:01:24.645
Brad: I don't know. You asked me what I know.

27
00:01:24.646 --> 00:01:29.507
Danny: Well, we know if we throw another rock, it will distract them.

28
00:01:29.508 --> 00:01:33.183
Brad: I'm fresh out of rocks.

29
00:01:33.184 --> 00:01:36.355
Danny: Hey, you've got your computer, don't you?

30
00:01:36.356 --> 00:01:40.723
Brad: I hadn't thought about

31
00:01:40.724 --> 00:01:43.106
it! It still

32
00:01:43.107 --> 00:01:46.666
works! Danny: Cool. You can throw it and distract them with

33
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:51.351
that. Brad: I'm not going to break my

34
00:01:51.352 --> 00:01:55.503
computer! There's got to be something I can do with my computer . . .

35
00:01:55.504 --> 00:01:57.372
I've got it! Danny:

36
00:01:57.373 --> 00:01:58.844
What?

37
00:01:58.845 --> 00:02:00.656
Brad: I can play a song!

38
00:02:00.657 --> 00:02:02.830
The mites will be curious.

39
00:02:02.832 --> 00:02:08.851
When they come to check it out, while they're here, we can go get the bullies. Danny:

40
00:02:08.852 --> 00:02:11.114
How will we get down from here? Brad:

41
00:02:11.115 --> 00:02:15.279
We'll have to jump. Danny:

42
00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.385
It's a long way down.

43
00:02:17.386 --> 00:02:27.317
We could hurt ourselves.

44
00:02:27.319 --> 00:02:33.866
Brad: Don't worry. I think we'll be all right.

45
00:02:33.867 --> 00:02:41.016
Danny: I sure hope you're right about this.

46
00:02:41.017 --> 00:02:43.775
Brad: Follow me. Run!

47
00:02:43.776 --> 00:02:48.800
Danny: Okay, now what?

48
00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:52.250
Brad: We're almost there.

49
00:02:52.251 --> 00:02:53.919
Grab this feather.

50
00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.071
We'll use it like a

51
00:02:56.073 --> 00:03:00.696
parachute. We're so tiny that we'll float softly to the ground.

52
00:03:00.697 --> 00:03:02.863
Danny: Okay, here we go.

53
00:03:02.864 --> 00:03:05.478
Brad: One, two, three!

54
00:03:05.479 --> 00:03:11.663
Danny: Now!

